+# PROJECT STATE — IntelliSchedule
+
+Last reviewed against the code after the security hardening round. Only statements backed by a test or a command are marked **Done**.
+
+## Status
+

+| Area | Status | Evidence |
+|---|---|---|
+| Type check | Done | `npm run lint` reports 0 errors (`strict: true`) |
+| Password hashing (bcrypt cost 12, scrypt/SHA-256 migration, rehash) | Done | `tests/password.test.ts` |
+| Cookie-only sessions, no tokens in JSON bodies | Done | `tests/hardening.test.ts` |
+| CSRF header + Origin check | Done | `tests/hardening.test.ts` |
+| CSP (own origin only for `connect-src`) | Done | `server.ts` helmet config; styles still need `'unsafe-inline'` for React inline styles |
+| Email verification before first sign-in | Done | `tests/pre_registration_takeover.test.ts`, e2e |
+| Typed one-time tokens, anti-enumeration timing | Done | `tests/one_time_tokens.test.ts`, `tests/timing_enumeration.test.ts` |
+| Role/ownership checks, student data allowlist | Done | `tests/hardening.test.ts`, e2e |
+| Solver (lab blocks, locks, protected slots, diagnostics) | Done | `tests/engine.test.ts` |
+| CI | Configured | `.github/workflows/ci.yml` (runs on push) |
+
+## Known gaps (not done)
+
+- **Backend architecture:** `server.ts` (in-memory users + Supabase Auth client + `supabaseStore.ts`) is the live server. It is large and should be split into modules.
+- **Persistence:** sessions, tokens, pending registrations and rate-limit buckets are stored in a local JSON file (`PERSISTENT_STATE_DIR`). A Postgres backend (migration `20261006000001_persistent_state.sql` already exists) is not wired in; this is unsafe with several instances or ephemeral disks.
+- **Session policy:** no idle/absolute timeout, no concurrent-session cap, no session rotation on role change.
+- **Solver:** heuristic with local search; no CP-SAT/ILP backend, and generation runs on the main thread (`src/server/jobWorker.ts` is not wired in).
+- **Password reset via Supabase client:** `LoginPageView` still contains a client-side Supabase recovery path alongside the server flow.
+- **Frontend:** single large bundle; no code splitting.
+- **Rate limits and the file store** are per-process.
+
